          %p
            %strong remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p the application to string theory here will have completely topological flavor
            %li
              %p defining certain terms in an action like Wess-Zumino-Witten term and chern-Simons term, these are nicely understood in terms of differential cohomology: observation goes back to Gawedzki
            %li
              %p in physics the forms are “currents” which say where charges are located, the class in real cohomology is the total charge
            %li
              %p in quantum physics this total charge has to be quantized (sit on a lattice inside the real cohomology)
            %li
              %p so the above pullback diagram says that classical charges are to be combined with quantization condition in order to give physical fields
          %h3#twistings_of_
